```c
if (diff > 0) {
    ndigits -= diff;
    memset(&out[ndigits - 1], 0, diff * sizeof(u64));
}
```
```c
memcpy((u8 *)&msd + sizeof(msd) - o, in, o);
```
Reason:
The first statement checks if there are not enough input bytes and, if so, initializes the most significant digits of the output array to zero, preventing the use of uninitialized values. This ensures that the output array is correctly filled even when the input is insufficient. The second statement remains unchanged but is now safe because the preceding check guarantees that the copying operation does not exceed the bounds of the input array.

